  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "debugtools-tools-modern-debug",
  "description": "Issue #11 closure: five shipped bounded tools driven LIVE from the real Chapter 2 map debug hub, with a clean debug-only boot (blank SRAM). Reuses the proven Fast Boot: Chapter 2 map-hub frame prefix to reach an interactive PlayerPhase map, opens the map hub (SELECT+L; hubOpenCount 1->2, sHubActive 0->1, registeredActionCount==9), then triggers each tool from its real hub row and proves an asserted semantic state effect plus a safe return to the hub, all via relocation-independent gDebugToolsProbe/gPlaySt/gBmSt scalars (never a pointer, framebuffer, or SRAM-hash oracle):\n 5 Unit Inspect/Edit: inspect resolves CHARACTER_EIRIKA (unitInspectTargetFound==1, curHP/maxHP both 16), a separate confirm applies Heal-to-Full (unitHealTransactionCount 0->1). Eirika is already at full HP at this runtime start, so the live proof is the confirmed-transaction postcondition; the byte-exact wounded->full HP mutation is proven by the real-source host test tools/gba-playtest/tests/c/debugtools_tools_driver.c.\n 6 Convoy Inspect/Edit: inspect samples GetConvoyItemCount()==0, a separate confirm adds a test item (convoyAddTransactionCount 0->1), and a re-inspect shows the count actually rose (convoyLastItemCount 0->1) -- a genuine in-scenario pre/post delta.\n 7 Flag/Chapter: inspect samples gPlaySt.chapterIndex==2 and the flag==0; a separate confirm toggles it (debugFlagToggleCount 0->1) with the flag value going 0->1.\n 8 RNG Inspect/Control: inspect samples the live RN seed (0x0000ee77); a separate confirm reseeds (rngReseedTransactionCount 0->1), and a re-inspect shows the seed actually changed (0x0000ee77 -> 0x0000690b) -- a genuine in-scenario pre/post delta.\n 9 Save Compatibility/State Inspect (read-only): inspect classifies SRAM (saveCompatLastState==SAVE_COMPAT_CURRENT/4, saveCompatInspectCount 0->1); its Back item is a pure cancel and the inspect count stays 1 with no mutation -- proving the inspector never writes.\nEach mutating tool mutates only after its own explicit confirm submenu item; each submenu returns cleanly to the hub (hubOpenCount rises 2->9, sHubActive re-toggles) and a final B closes the hub (sHubActive 1->0). The real map is then still interactive: a RIGHT press moves the player cursor (gBmSt.playerCursor.x 0x06->0x07) while the phase byte stays stable. Debug-only: the hub, tools, and gDebugToolsProbe writes are all compiled out of a release build (see the release negative sibling debugtools-tools-modern-release.json).",
